#N canvas 0 33 1440 711 12;
#X text 20 10 paulstretch~ <array> <stretch>: plays the array stretched (default 10x) like Audacity's Paulstretch. Window 8192 samples \, 4x overlap. Each block reads a Hann-windowed chunk \, keeps the FFT magnitudes \, randomizes the phases (L and R separately) and overlap-adds. Loops. L reads the left array and R the right one. With one array both read it (a mono sound comes out wide).;
#X text 479 9 messages: set <left> [<right>] | stretch <f> | pos <samples>. Right outlet: bang each time it reaches the end (and loops).;
#X obj 820 150 block~ 8192 4;
#X obj 20 150 inlet;
#X obj 20 180 route set stretch pos;
